2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T20:21:54-07:00","id":1122181,"title":"","content":"Strangely enough, I think Sun Wukong might actually end up with more friends than enemies from other pantheons.<br /> <br /> For someone who made such a huge mess in Heaven, he was able to call in divine assistance on numerous occasions even when those divinities had no connections whatsoever to the monster of the week. For example, Erlang threw him a feast before helping him out with a family of river dragons without Sun Wukong actually having to do anything besides ask, which was rather odd considering that the two had fought a vicious battle on the Mountain of Flowers and Fruit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T21:16:06-07:00","id":1122206,"title":"","content":"Sutekh is the god of foreigners. I'm sure our red-headed friends has a lot of contacts, if not necessarily buddies; I feel like the Netjer as a whole are a little stoic for most of the other Pantheons' tastes. Maybe they get alone well with the Teotl? Both know the all-consuming importance of the mortals working towards upholding the proper order of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 07-29-2017, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T09:58:08-07:00","id":1122380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1121341-who-do-you-think-would-be-buddies-amomg-the-gods?p=1122206#post1122206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sutekh is the god of foreigners. I'm sure our red-headed friends has a lot of contacts, if not necessarily buddies; I feel like the Netjer as a whole are a little stoic for most of the other Pantheons' tastes. Maybe they get alone well with the Teotl? Both know the all-consuming importance of the mortals working towards upholding the proper order of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that I think about it, both pantheons also place a large importance on protecting the sun, so I could definitely see a bond forming over that as well. In general though, with the Netjer being one of the oldest pantheons, I would say they'd probably look at everyone other than the Anunna as young upstarts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13472-~nkf~","name":"~NKF~","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T00:27:01-07:00","id":1122639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1121341-who-do-you-think-would-be-buddies-amomg-the-gods?p=1121598#post1121598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see various death gods getting together to gamble over who get's various non-religious celebrities' souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually had that happen in a game I ran once. More commonly, I have groups of trickster deities gambling for various stolen goods. I call that semi-regular event &quot;Gods Playing Poker&quot;, and it usually happens at least once in every world featuring the old Gods in the modern day, regardless of game system. I pretty much treat all the tricksters as being both friends and rivals with each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T15:28:28-07:00","id":1123199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shadryx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1121341-who-do-you-think-would-be-buddies-amomg-the-gods?p=1121506#post1121506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thor, Heracles and Cuchulain could party together until the whole building came down around them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly have this mental image of the three of them along with Chango, Monster Slayer and Born-for-Water, Takemikauchi, and maybe Durga as some sort of biker gang.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T20:49:30-07:00","id":1123300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1121341-who-do-you-think-would-be-buddies-amomg-the-gods?p=1123199#post1123199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I honestly have this mental image of the three of them along with Chango, Monster Slayer and Born-for-Water, Takemikauchi, and maybe Durga as some sort of biker gang.</div> </div> </div> </div>Durga actually can't stand those guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T21:12:04-07:00","id":1123303,"title":"","content":"Ya, Durga's usually more stately Queen of the Universe than biker gang member... you could try Kali, who in at least <i>some</i> of her Aspects would probably fit <i>way</i> better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T22:01:37-07:00","id":1123310,"title":"","content":"I wonder how well Ptah and Hephaestus get on, both being the engineering type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T22:12:52-07:00","id":1123313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1121341-who-do-you-think-would-be-buddies-amomg-the-gods?p=1123310#post1123310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how well Ptah and Hephaestus get on, both being the engineering type.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'm thinking they're friendly enough, but they have a definite competitive streak with each other. I see a lot of one-upping going on in that relationship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T22:37:08-07:00","id":1123320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1121341-who-do-you-think-would-be-buddies-amomg-the-gods?p=1123313#post1123313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI'm thinking they're friendly enough, but they have a definite competitive streak with each other. I see a lot of one-upping going on in that relationship.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ptah probably has a little bit of an ego, on account of his Scion Imhotep being one of the greatest architects of all time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T04:59:35-07:00","id":1123405,"title":"","content":"Zeus and Shango are probably god-king bros.<br /> <br /> Dionysus is everyone's favourite drug dealer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T22:53:18-07:00","id":1124188,"title":"","content":"Loki and Hermes:<br /> <br /> Hermes kills Apollo's sheep, makes a musical instrument out of them, entertains Apollo when he comes looking for revenge, and is rewarded with godhood.<br /> <br /> That's a kind of trickery that Loki can appreciate!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T23:29:00-07:00","id":1124198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1121341-who-do-you-think-would-be-buddies-amomg-the-gods?p=1124188#post1124188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loki and Hermes:<br /> <br /> Hermes kills Apollo's sheep, makes a musical instrument out of them, entertains Apollo when he comes looking for revenge, and is rewarded with godhood.<br /> <br /> That's a kind of trickery that Loki can appreciate!</div> </div> </div> </div>1st edition generally supposed the default dynamic between gods of different pantheons with a lot of purview or role (what we'd now call Calling) overlap was rivalry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\